The layout audit (login 100svh, 44px hit targets, onboarding flow) was
run twice as a throwaway gitignored script before anything caught these
bug classes in code — and the raw-slug leak was only found because the
manual scan happened to look. This makes the audit permanent:

scripts/browser-smoke.mjs checks, against running servers, that
- login content stays inside 100svh in portrait (EN and FA, 390/360px)
  with the legal line in the viewport without scrolling;
- NO dotted ESPN slug ever appears in visible text on the feed, a real
  match page, a real team page, or the unmapped xxx.test_cup deep link
  — the hard gate that pins the leagueScope fix;
- the reset sheet's footer buttons stay >=44px and unclipped;
- onboarding advances pick -> Continue, and Skip lands on the feed.

Every page runs under a throwaway numeric ?devUser= identity (the
server's verifyDevToken accepts dev:<digits> only) so favorites picked
by one check cannot leak into the next, and data pollution cannot make
the suite red. CI runs it after Install/Seed with a bundled chromium
(installed --no-save: browsers are bulky and the suite does not need
them for unit tests); the suite waits for both servers itself, so no
extra wait tooling. 22 checks, green, repeatable locally via
SMOKE_CHANNEL=msedge npm run smoke.

